{
  "_why": "Role track for EDM / WIRE-CUT, a new trade (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #7, sheet 16). fam_edm_wirecut binds NCO 7223.2800 'Die Copying Machine Operator / Die Sinking Electric Discharge Machine Operator' at job-domain specificity 50; every other 7223 code stays on fam_machining, and the tool room keeps its own EDM chips.",
  "_scope": "THE SPARK-EROSION MACHINES, NOT THE TOOL ROOM. A tool maker who also runs a wire-cut is a Tool & Die Maker (his EDM row lives in qp_tool_die_making); this trade is the operator, setter and programmer whose job IS the wire-cut / sinker EDM, in a tool room or a job shop.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS edm_experience, asked FIRST. Its options carry value_number ONLY: pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, and a value_text would turn every gte below into a string compare that is false forever (the #776 defect).",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Easy is 2 trade items + at most 1 confirm; Medium adds 2 (machine, brand); Advanced adds 3 (program source, tolerance / finish, work). Worst case 2 + 1 + 2 + 3 = 8 trade asks.",
  "_sheet": "READ OFF CEO LAUNCH PLAN PACK v1 SHEET 16 (a new trade, no ratified page). Section title 'EDM, machines & capability'. Its rows are Machines, Brands, Program source, Tolerance / finish and Work, and every row has exactly one question here.",
  "pack_id": "qp_edm_wirecut",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_edm_wirecut",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "v1 (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #7): new trade. Easy/Medium/Advanced tiers; 6-band experience; sheet-16 level ladder (Trainee/Operator/Setter/Setter-cum-Programmer/Supervisor, mandatory); 2 separating confirms, the sheet's questions verbatim: setter, and setter-cum-programmer; supervisor by rule. Medium Q6 machine, Q7 brand; Advanced Q9 program source, Q10 tolerance / finish, Q11 work (taper, 4-axis, electrode making, carbide), gated years OR rung. Deviations recorded: Q10's bands are the grinding / tool-room tolerance bands (the sheet names the row, not its chips); no fresher items and no per-trade ITI row (Q12 is the shared qp_universal block; 3D / PLC precedent for a new trade). Drafted for owner review (Prakash).",
